# Model Tier Routing — Porteos Intelligence

Before starting any task, select the appropriate model tier. The goal is to use the cheapest model that can reliably complete the task without mistakes.

## Tier 1 — claude-3-5-haiku (fast, cheap, use by default)

Use for anything touching only ONE of these files in isolation:
- `MarketBenchmarks.swift` — adding cities, adjusting rates
- `MarketFeedRegistry.swift` — adding feeds, aliases
- `DealPropertyTypes.swift` — adding property types
- `DealTemplates.swift` — adding/editing templates
- `PorteosGlossary.swift` — glossary entries
- `LLMAnalysisService.swift` — prompt text edits only (not routing logic)
- `UnitSystemService.swift` — adding currency/country mappings
- `PorteosScoreCalculator.swift` — weight/threshold adjustments only
- `BrowserExtension/**` — JavaScript scraper updates
- `BetaGuide.md` or any `.md` file — documentation
- Any single-view label, color token, or copy change

## Tier 2 — claude-sonnet-4-5 (balanced, use for most feature work)

Use when the task touches 2–5 files OR involves logic changes:
- Dashboard views (`RealEstateDashboardView`, `HospitalityDashboardView`, etc.)
- `NewsAggregatorService.swift` + `MarketFeedRegistry.swift` together
- `SensitivityAnalysisBlock.swift` — calculation changes
- `PreloadReviewSheet.swift`, `BatchTriageView.swift`
- `PDFReportGenerator.swift` — layout changes
- `MarketTrendGrid.swift` — metric changes
- `GeocodingService.swift` — query or fallback logic
- `NavigationPane.swift` — UI additions
- `SettingsView.swift` — new settings sections
- `CompactDealInspector.swift`, `DealMediaGalleryView.swift`
- Bug fixes in files under 600 lines with clear scope
- Browser extension: adding a new portal scraper

## Tier 3 — claude-sonnet-4-6 (frontier, use sparingly)

ONLY use for tasks involving these files or categories:

**High-risk files (never touch with Tier 1/2):**
- `FullDealEditSheet.swift` (1,274 lines — complex state, all model fields)
- `AIVibePanel.swift` (1,149 lines — SwiftUI identity, @Observable, scoring)
- `AIAnalysisService.swift` (989 lines — signal pipeline, LLM routing)
- `AppShell.swift` — core layout and window management
- `PropertyDeal.swift` — SwiftData schema changes (data loss risk)
- `DealHistoryManager.swift` — snapshot/undo system
- `EmailMonitorService.swift` — IMAP + async + Keychain
- `DealIngestionServer.swift` — HTTP server protocol changes

**High-risk categories:**
- Any SwiftData `@Relationship` or `@Model` change
- Security: Keychain storage, API key handling, network auth
- Concurrency: `async`/`await`, `@MainActor`, actor isolation
- Multi-window: `WindowManager`, `ProfileWindowView`, `WindowGroup` scenes
- Onboarding flow (new screens touching AppShell)
- Swift 6 concurrency compliance fixes
- Anything that cascades across 5+ files

## Decision rule

```
Single file, data/config/copy only?  → Tier 1 (Haiku)
2-5 files, logic changes, clear scope? → Tier 2 (Sonnet 4.5)
High-risk file OR schema/security/concurrency? → Tier 3 (Sonnet 4.6)
```

## Cost context

- Tier 1: ~$0.05/session
- Tier 2: ~$0.50/session  
- Tier 3: ~$3–5/session

Target: 60% Tier 1 · 30% Tier 2 · 10% Tier 3 = ~$5–15/month
